WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.040
Now one of the most respected scientists

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.720
who was also a spiritualist was this gentleman here

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.580
who's doing some exercise in his home.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.340
Sir Oliver Lodge.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.800
Who very much pursued both electromagnetic research

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.840
and the study of spirits and telepathy 
as two sides of the same coin.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.380
He's today famous for being one of the pioneers

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.360
of radio. As well as inventing the spark plug

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.360
and the loud speaker.

00:00:24.362 --> 00:00:27.000
So he invented the device called the "coherer"

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.460
which was like a simple electromagnetic wave detector.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.720
And spent much of his later career

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.460
competing with Marconi in commercializing the radio.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.580
And he was an active memberof the 
SPR (Society for Psychical Research).

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.040
But he was very respected.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.880
He gave a lot of public lectures. And he was seen as

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.600
this very very reliable scientific figure.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.160
So when Frederic Myers, one of the founders of SPR

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.220
that we met earlier, decided to do an experiment

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.020
as he felt the end of his life was approaching.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:00.640
He gave Lodge a sealed letter

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.940
that was only to be opened after Myers death.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.200
And he was going to try to pass on a message

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.580
from beyond that was supposed to be matched

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.940
to the contents of the letter.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:16.540
And it seemed like the experiment was successful.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.800
In 1901 a group of women at the very highest level

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.620
of British society started receiving
messages from Myers

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.480
by "automatic writing." And at least according
to some interpretations

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.063
the messages matched the contents of  the letter

00:01:30.063 --> 00:01:32.240
that Lodge had been given.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:39.720
One of the key mediums was Alice Fleming on the left;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.200
the sister of the famous writer Rudyard Kipling.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.720
Alice co-authored some of Kipling's early Indian tales.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.500
As a side note Kipling also wrote a great
short story called "The Wireless"

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.180
which is about contacting the afterlife with radio.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:59.760
Another medium receiving messages from Myers

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.960
was Winifred Coombe Tennant, up there on the right.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.680
Also a very remarkable woman.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.980
A suffragist, a Member of Parliament and later 
the British delegate to the League of Nations.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.200
There were a few others as well.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.600
And all the letters from Myers were shared

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.380
amongst this very elite group.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.900
The hub of the group was the moustached gentleman

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.840
on the bottom left, Arthur Balfour,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.140
who had been the president of SPR

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.380
and at the time when these letters were arriving

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.360
he was the Prime Minister of Britain.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.260
And later he got the nickname "Bloody Balfour" for

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.120
cruelly putting down unrest in Northern Ireland.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.500
And he was the one who signed the declaration to

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.580
found the state of Palestine. So a pretty important guy.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.280
His brother Gerald in the middle 
was equally accomplished.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.220
And they had a third brother, Francis,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.533
who died very young at the age of thirty,

00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:57.140
many years before while climbing Mont Blanc.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.480
And he was known for his talent in biology.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.163
People said he would be the successor to Darwin.

00:03:03.163 --> 00:03:05.600
But he died before he could realize that.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.640
In any case this group

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.900
circulated all these letters arriving from Frederic Myers

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.880
from beyond, from the afterlife, via automatic writing.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.040
And it was kind of shared hypertext, if you like.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.960
They kept all this very secret.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.240
and these letters were all interconnected

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:24.360
seemingly even though different people received them.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.100
There were symbols that recurred

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.180
from classics from the Bible from Shakespeare

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.780
and so on. And there were so many interconnections

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.920
that ultimately the group became entirely convinced

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:33.940
that this was real.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.020
This was Myers talking to them from the afterlife.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.400
Other people started talking to them from the afterlife

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.760
including May Lyttelton who'd been sort of this lost love

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.220
of Arthur Balfour when he was young,

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.800
who had also died very young.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.480
And also Francis Balfour, the third Balfour brother.

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.080
And there was this big picture this plan or

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.180
a story that started to emerge from the letters.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.780
And so what Myers was saying

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.480
was that a kind of Darwinian evolution

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.140
continued in the afterlife. And

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.720
as Myers and Francis Balfour had entered the afterlife

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.480
they had gotten a lot smarter.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.580
And there had been a sort of scientific revolution

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.940
in the afterlife.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:18.140
People in the afterlife had perfected
the engineering of souls.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.900
In fact Francis Balfour

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.660
was leading a team of spirit scientists

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.440
who were designing a perfect soul.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.480
A sort of perfectly engineered spirit child

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:33.540
whose task would be to deliver humanity from chaos.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.000
And of course this perfect soul only needed a vessel

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.260
to be incarnated into.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.680
Now again a bit of context: this was 1912 at this point.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.900
The British elite had this kind of widespread sense

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.360
of crisis approaching. Chaos in the world.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.740
There were socialists and anarchists and feminists

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.320
and suffragists and sort of unrest in Europe. And all

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.860
these alliances unravelling.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.420
So it was pretty clear that somebody

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.760
somebody needed to save the world.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.980
So two members of this group,

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.500
Sir Arthur's living brother Gerald (in the middle)

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.620
and Winifred up on the right,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.740
sort of took one for the team and they had an affair.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.880
They were instructed by the spirits to have an affair.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.240
And Winifred's much older husband actually

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:20.740
knew about it, but sort of maintained stiff upper lip

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:22.080
and said nothing about it.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.100
And Winifred got pregnant and gave birth

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.880
to the vessel of this perfect engineered soul.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:32.120
And I just can't help thinking how

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.300
remarkable this story is.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.800
This is happening at the highest levels

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.740
of British politics and society

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:42.780
combining all these ideas about eugenics and evolution

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.020
and engineering

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.300
applied in this very otherworldly context.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.740
So here is the spirit child.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.820
At the age of one, and then at the age of thirty.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.900
And he was called Henry Coombe-Tennant.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.920
Born in 1913. And as far as we know

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.520
he wasn't the Messiah. He didn't save the world

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.960
from chaos unfortunately.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:06.389
But he did have a pretty interesting life.

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:07.880
He studied in Cambridge.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:12.140
He met Wittgenstein; taught by Ludwig Wittgenstein,

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.220
the famous philosopher.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.320
Fought in World War II and got imprisoned.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.880
Escaped a German prison camp by himself.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.560
Fled across Europe.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.820
Ended up working for the British intelligence service,

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.460
for MI6, together with Kim Philby

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:30.380
who would later be revealed as one of the most

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:33.120
one of the deepest Soviet moles,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.340
double agents of all time.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.660
And it was really Henry's life that kind of made me

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.600
decide that "Summerland" had to be a spy story.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.040
He was an inspiration for one of the protagonists.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.120
Now later on Henry's life sort of quieted down.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.620
But in the 50s he did try to contact his mother,

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.600
Winifred, through a medium.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.800
Probably to complain about the kind of
weird circumstances of his birth

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.480
or too high expectations.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.160
And it's not clear if he succeeded.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.420
But soon after that he did go away 
to become a Catholic monk

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.540
and lived for the rest of his life in solitude. So...

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.680
It is actually the kind of biography

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.880
you can never put in fiction

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.000
because nobody would believe it.

